The full paper confirms the intended witness problem is coefficient-level min-plus convolution factorization, not equality merely as piecewise-linear functions. The paper’s security section is cautious: it cites NP-hardness but also warns that generic endpoint-zero polynomials are likely irreducible and that safe key generation is unresolved. I’m now checking the cited factorization theorem and attack paper, because those details determine whether random planted products are genuinely in the hard regime.
